// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'defaultDataset'. Valid alternatives: ['projectId', 'instanceId', 'databaseId', 'proxyHost', 'proxyPort']
//
// `defaultDataset:` on a Spanner specification. Spanner and BigQuery are both Google specs in
// the same section, both address a `projectId`, and both carry `proxyHost`/`proxyPort` -- three
// of Spanner's five tokens are spelled identically to three of BigQuery's four. The fourth is
// not shared in either direction: `defaultDataset` is BigQuery-only and `instanceId` /
// `databaseId` are Spanner-only.
//
// A near-total overlap with a disjoint remainder is the configuration most likely to be
// collapsed by a rewrite, and collapsing it costs nothing visible: the merged parser accepts
// every positive fixture in ../fixtures/ and produces a well-formed protocol object for a
// specification that cannot exist.
//
// The two lexers share no tokens -- each declares its own PROJECT_ID -- so the overlap is
// spelling only. See ./neg-bigquery-missing-project-id.pure for the other side.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::SpannerDefaultDataset
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Spanner;
  specification: Spanner
  {
    defaultDataset: 'd';
    projectId: 'p';
    instanceId: 'i';
    databaseId: 'db';
  };
  auth: Test;
}
